EXTENSION "ArM5_Legends_of_Hermes_FortunatasIslandOfBoundSpirits_MonocaudusAMagicalServant" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Legends of Hermes - Monocaudus, a Magical Servant"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-08"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Legends_of_Hermes_Core_Ext"

    # Monocaudus, a Magical Servant (Chapter Three: Fortunata’s Island of Bound Spirits, p63): one being, its printed stat lines verbatim fields.

    #t7d42dbe8b7c40b27152e14 ^"Monocaudus, a Magical Servant" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tOmeyTfuLwkiC9FmXsz8PTO6 ^"Creature"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Might Realm" STRING "Magic" FIXED
            ^"Might" INTEGER 25
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Characteristics (Man)" STRING "Int 0, Per +1, Pre –1, Com +1, Str +2, Sta +3, Dex +2, Qik 2"
            ^"Characteristics (Serpent)" STRING "Int 0, Per +1, Pre –1, Com +1, Str +6, Sta +3, Dex +2, Qik 0"
            ^"Printed Size" STRING "+1 (Man), +2 (Serpent)"
            ^"Confidence" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Magical Animal, Size +2 (free) or Large (free); Animal Ken, Improved Characteristics (×3), Improved Soak (x2), Puissant Brawl, Sharp Ears, Tough, Wilderness Sense; Magical Monster, Monstrous Appearance, Plagued by Supernatural Entity (Lucida); Disfigured (Tattooed all over)"
            ^"Magical Qualities and Inferiorities" STRING "Gift of Speech, Personal Power (Human Form), Improved Abilities (x4), Improved Attack (x2), Improved Damage (x2), Improved Defense, Improved Might (x5), Personal Power (Human Form); Slow Power (Human Form)"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Dodge (Man): Init: +2, Attack –, Defense +9, Damage – Fist (Man): Init: +2, Attack +14, Defense +12, Damage +8 Bite (Man): Init: +2, Attack +9, Defense +9, Damage +2 Dodge (Serpent): Init: +0, Attack –, Defense +7, Damage – Fist (Serpent): Init: +0, Attack +14, Defense +10, Damage +12 Bite (Serpent): Init: +0, Attack +9, Defense +7, Damage +6 Constrict (Serpent): Init: +0, Attack +12, Defense +7, Damage – Monocaudus’ “Man Form” is an active magical power, and so his attacks must penetrate Magic Resistance. In his natural serpent form, he does not need to penetrate, which may surprise the unwary magus, thinking it an assumed form. Constriction is based on the grappling rules (ArM5 page 174). If he wraps his tail around a victim and maintains the constriction, the victim suffers Deprivation from lack of air, while Monocaudus is free to strike or bite the victim or another."
            ^"Soak" INTEGER 10
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties (Man)" STRING "–1 (1-6), –3 (7-12), –5 (13-18), Incapacitated (19-14)"
            ^"Wound Penalties (Serpent)" STRING "–1 (1-7), –3 (8-14), –5 (15-21), Incapacitated (22-28)"
            ^"Vis" STRING "5 Animal, in his tattoos."
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Monocaudus’ true form is that of a great serpent with the arms, chest and head of a man. His skin is not scaled like a snake, but rather covered in tattoos. He is bound by sustained magical command to serve Fortunata and to assume human form, the better to perform as a household slave."
            ^"Source" STRING "Legends of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 63
        }
        PERSONALITY_TRAITS {
            "Monstrous" +3
            "Resentful" +3
            "Bitter" +2
        }
        ABILITIES {
            "Animal Ken" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "serpents"
            "Awareness" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "alertness"
            "Athletics" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "run"
            "Brawl" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "fist"
            "Carouse" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "drunken stories"
            "Chirurgy" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "crude tools"
            "Concentration" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "when scolded"
            "Greek" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "curses"
            "Guile" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "elaborate lies"
            "Intrigue" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "malicious schemes"
            "Island Lore" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "history"
            "Italian" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "sailors"
            "Latin" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "orders"
            "Magic Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "creatures"
            "Mediterranean Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "nearby islands"
            "Wilderness Sense" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "islands"
        }
        POWERS {
            #t770f29aaf0ad10158832c0 ^"Human Form (Legends of Hermes)" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Printed Name" STRING "Human Form"
                    ^"Cost" STRING "1 point"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "-2"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "Monocaudus may (and is generally forced to) assume human form, which lasts for Sun duration or until he wills it to end. His human form loses the Serpent’s Size +2 (and the Str +4, Qik –2 that brings), but has the Large Virtue (Size +1, but no characteristic modifier)."
            }
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Fortunata defeated the ancient serpent Monocaudus, enemy of Lucida, and bound him as a slave, commanding him to perform the most menial tasks. He still lurks around the old villa, and makes token observance of his duties (such as collecting firewood), as he fears that Fortunata may yet return and punish him for his idleness. He resents his general condition and his binding, and curses Fortunata and Lucida to any who will listen — chiefly the minor spirits of the island, though they understand little of what he says.\n\nHe is often chastised and browbeaten by Lucida, but to little effect. Lucida can only remind Monocaudus of the ancient binding words, and of the future punishments which Fortunata will surely inflict, but has no magical power to force him to obey. Such haranguing only fuels his resentment.\n\nIn the long absence of Fortunata, her memory faded and Monocaudus may attempt to temporarily ignore her commands, either rebelling or assuming his natural form. To do this he must roll Stamina + appropriate Personality Trait against an Ease Factor of 12.\n\nThe curious consequence of his magically enforced human form is that attacks by his human form must penetrate Magic Resistance, but in his natural, monstrous form he does not need to penetrate. The unwary magus may be surprised by this. Lulled by their success at ignoring his fists, they witness his magical transformation and assume they can still resist his blows.\n\n[Monocaudus is designed using the design rules for “Dragons As Characters”, see *Realms of Power: Magic*, page 74, including the free base Size +2, and the constriction attack.]"
    }

}
